# TASK-AI-158 — root cause #2: switch blocklists to allowlists (3 findings)

1. WHERE: tools/ctx-tools/smoke.py:76 sanitize_secret_payload (+ every place it prints server errors / writes smoke-results.json).
   WRONG: `Authorization: Basic dXNlcjpwYXNz` → `Authorization: [REDACTED] dXNlcjpwYXNz`; any blocklist of key names/values leaks a new shape.
   GOAL (no secrets in logs/snapshots): ALLOWLIST output. For a JSON-RPC error record ONLY `code` (int) and a fixed category string you choose from the code; never print or store `message` or `data` from the server. For success record only tool names/counts.
   VERIFY: test: error {code:-32603, message:"Authorization: Basic dXNlcjpwYXNz", data:{access_token:"t"}} → stderr and smoke-results.json contain neither `dXNlcjpwYXNz` nor `t"`.
2. WHERE: scripts/ai/pack-context.mjs:184 validateOutputPath.
   WRONG: `--out ".GIT"` on a case-insensitive filesystem bypasses the case-sensitive `.git` checks and overwrites the gitdir pointer.
   GOAL: ALLOWLIST the destination: output must resolve (realpath of the parent, compared case-insensitively on win32/darwin) inside ONE fixed output directory (e.g. `<repo>/.context-packs/` or the existing default dir the tool already uses); anything else is refused. Also refuse any path segment equal to `.git` case-insensitively.
   VERIFY: tests: `--out .GIT` refused; `--out docs/x.md` refused; default/allowed path accepted.
3. WHERE: docs/product-spec/work-items/TASK-AI-158.md:143 (Current review repair evidence).
   WRONG: claims all CI gates were verified, while CI was still pending at that SHA.
   GOAL: the Work Item never asserts CI results; replace with "CI: see PR checks at the reviewed SHA" and list only local commands with their real output.
   VERIFY: python docs/product-spec/scripts/validate_docs.py passes.
   Run: python tools/ctx-tools/test_smoke.py (or pytest), node --test on pack-context tests, pnpm format:check, pnpm run security:secrets.

